  factId: S3_F02
  stageId: 3
  topicId: heat
  title: The urban heat island
  body: "Concrete, asphalt and buildings soak up the sun's heat and give it back
    slowly, and a city has few trees for shade. That makes cities hotter than the
    countryside around them. Metro Manila's surface temperature rose about 0.18 \xB0C
    a year from 1997 to 2019 as the city spread."
